# Router tests that cannot hold when a connection pooler sits between the router
# and the shards (make regress_odyssey). Everything else in schedule/router runs
# unchanged, against the same expected outputs.
#
# copy_to: after draining a COPY ... TO STDOUT the router sends a CopyDone of its
# own to every shard (copyToExecutor in router/relay/executor.go). In COPY-out
# the frontend is not supposed to send that message at all; postgres tolerates
# it, odyssey rejects it with "unexpected message type 'c' for client not in
# xproto mode". The check arrived in yandex/odyssey fa440cd ("correct support for
# Copy in xproto"), so the test still passed on 1.5.1-rc2 and fails on 1.5.1.
copy_to
